  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening One Health and Biosecurity for National and Producer Resilience ? Preventing National and Global Health Threats</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is structured around three key outcomes:
1.	Enhanced interoperability and effectiveness of animal and plant pests and disease (APPD) early warning and information exchange systems linking animal health, human health and the environment in target countries: One Health early warning and information systems (One Health intelligence) on APPDs including zoonotic diseases at the human-animal-environment interface are developed at global, regional and national level. 
2.	Improved resilience of agrifood systems to disease threats through national and community level implementation of a Progressive One Health Management Pathway for Biosecurity (PMP-B): Progressive One Health biosecurity management approaches co-developed between public and private stakeholders, and implemented to progress in health and SPS standards.
3.	One Health competencies of animal health workforce strengthened through regionally and locally adapted training and knowledge platforms: network of regional VLCs supports the roll-out of competency-based training systems to ensure animal health workforce at local, national and regional level acquire knowledge and skills on One Health, improved biosecurity and early warning and information exchange systems.</narrative>
  </description>
